`RefractState` extends the engine's `GameState`, so an instance also carries the
framework's own `world`, `players`, `phase`, and `elapsed`. Refract's screens
run on `screen` rather than on the match phase: the mode never calls
`setPhase`, so `phase` stays `"waiting"` and `elapsed` stays `0`, and the one
player the mode adds is `players[0]`, whose controller is where input is read.

